    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://erlangen-crm.org/240307/P67_refers_to"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/golem/ontology#G5_Narrative_Event"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/TemporalRelations.owl#temporally-included-in">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>temporally included in</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n43ae1f1b737245548d0fdb39e48725cdb25">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/ExtendedDnS.owl#setting-for"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/DOLCE-Lite.owl#time-interval"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/ExtendedDnS.owl#setting">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment>In GOLEM, links a narrative setting (G12) to various elements such as location (G13), time, character (G1), object (G16), or event (G5).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>The relation between a situation and the entities that constitute it. (At least some of, or all) such entities must be classified by concepts defined by the description that the situation is supposed to satisfy ([DOLCE-Lite-Plus, 2005](https://www.w3.org/2001/sw/BestPractices/WNET/DLP3941_daml.html)).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">setting</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n43ae1f1b737245548d0fdb39e48725cdb46">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/ExtendedDnS.owl#plays"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/golem/ontology#G6_Relationship_Role"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n43ae1f1b737245548d0fdb39e48725cdb54">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/golem/ontology#G5_Narrative_Event"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n43ae1f1b737245548d0fdb39e48725cdb51">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/TemporalRelations.owl#follows"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:nodeID="n43ae1f1b737245548d0fdb39e48725cdb52"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso">
    <rdfs:comment>Further information about the subject resource.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"/>
    <rdfs:label>seeAlso</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/CommonSenseMapping.owl#duration">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment>In GOLEM, indicates that a narrative event (G5) has a specific duration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>duration</rdfs:label>
    <skos:example>The Battle of Hogwarts (G5) has *duration* several hours (time-interval).</skos:example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="n43ae1f1b737245548d0fdb39e48725cdb12">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://erlangen-crm.org/240307/P127i_has_narrower_term"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://erlangen-crm.org/240307/E55_Type"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/SpatialRelations.owl#participant-place-of">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">participant place of</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/DOLCE-Lite.owl#proper-part">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment>In GOLEM, indicates that an entity is proper part of a larger entity. For example, a child location (G13) is proper part of a larger parent location (G13).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">proper part</rdfs:label>
    <skos:example>Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows (Rowling, 2007) (F1) has proper part Hyleme “Harry’s triumph, as Voldemort dies from his rebounded curse” (G9).</skos:example>
    <skos:example>Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry (G13) has proper part Forbidden Forest (G13).</skos:example>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
